What the results show beyond the ranking ([patterns](docs/benchmarks/multihop-rag.md#patterns-across-the-runs)):

- **Temporal questions are the hardest**: the retrieving systems average {{ (temporal | sum / temporal | length) | score }} on them, and {{ pat.hard.none_by_category.get("temporal_query", 0) }} of the {{ pat.hard.none }} questions no system answers well are temporal.
- **The null queries separate the systems most.** The frameworks' tutorial pipelines answer many of them anyway ({{ fw_null | min | score }} to {{ fw_null | max | score }}, against {{ cats["null_query"]["hybrid_default"] | score }} for `hybrid_default`), which is most of their gap.
- **Spending more per question does not buy a better answer**: across the {{ retrieving | length }} retrieving systems, cost per question and answer score have a rank correlation of {{ rank_correlation(retrieving, "avg_cost_per_question", "answer_score") | score }}.
